    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742-a6">

                <pb facs="0815" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg717"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex 5]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister of Communications</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yeh Kung-cho</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Representatives of the
                            Russo-Asiatic Bank</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: By your letter of today, you ask me as
                    follows:— <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“As has been agreed in the course of the negotiations leading up to the
                            Agreement signed today, we would be grateful if Your Excellency would be
                            so good as to confirm that instructions will immediately be given to the
                            President of the Chinese Eastern Railway to convene at Peking, during
                            the course of October, a general meeting of the shareholders of the
                            Company, which will legally name its Board of Management (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Pravlenia</hi>) and will proceed to the
                            discussion of the reorganization of the line upon a commercial
                            basis.</p>
                        <p>It remains understood that, in the future, a general meeting will take
                            place annually in accordance with the Statutes of the Company.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of this communication and to confirm
                    to you my agreement upon all these points.</p>
                <p>Pray accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Yeh Kung-cho</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
